geometric-correction-fbb36892.conceptual_definition:
The equation $ U^{
u} 
abla_{
u} U^{\mu} = 0 $, often referred to as the geodesic equation in its geometric form, describes the motion of a free particle in spacetime. It states that the four-velocity of a particle remains parallel to itself along its trajectory. In the absence of external forces, particles follow paths of extremal proper time, which are called geodesics. This equation is a fundamental tenet of general relativity, encapsulating the principle that gravity is not a force but a manifestation of spacetime curvature.

